---
import './design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from './SketchSheet.astro';
---
<figure id="rejoining-records" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface rejoin wide" aria-labelledby="rejoin-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Preserving the association</span>
  <h3 id="rejoin-title">Keep enough information to put the pieces back</h3>
  <p>O13’s first line is a mug at €20; its second is a bowl at €24. Suppose we separate their products and prices. Each line below is a match a join would make.</p>
  <div class="join-options">
    <div>
      <h4>Keep order_id and line_no on both sides</h4>
      <div class="match-pair"><span>Product</span><span>Agreed price</span></div>
      <div class="match-drawing">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 25 Q45 23 100 25 M0 75 Q55 77 100 75" /></svg>
        <div class="match-column"><SketchSheet tone="blue"><small>O13 · line&nbsp;1</small><strong>P7 · mug</strong></SketchSheet><SketchSheet tone="blue"><small>O13 · line&nbsp;2</small><strong>P8 · bowl</strong></SketchSheet></div>
        <div class="match-column"><SketchSheet tone="teal"><small>O13 · line&nbsp;1</small><strong>€20</strong></SketchSheet><SketchSheet tone="teal"><small>O13 · line&nbsp;2</small><strong>€24</strong></SketchSheet></div>
      </div>
      <p class="join-result"><strong>2 matches</strong><br />Each product finds its own line’s price.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>Keep only order_id on both sides</h4>
      <div class="match-pair"><span>Product</span><span>Agreed price</span></div>
      <div class="match-drawing">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 25 Q45 23 100 25 M0 75 Q55 77 100 75" /><path class="false-match" d="M0 25 C40 25 60 75 100 75 M0 75 C40 75 60 25 100 25" /></svg>
        <div class="match-column"><SketchSheet tone="blue"><small>O13</small><strong>P7 · mug</strong></SketchSheet><SketchSheet tone="blue"><small>O13</small><strong>P8 · bowl</strong></SketchSheet></div>
        <div class="match-column"><SketchSheet tone="amber"><small>O13</small><strong>€20</strong></SketchSheet><SketchSheet tone="amber"><small>O13</small><strong>€24</strong></SketchSheet></div>
      </div>
      <p class="join-result wrong"><strong>4 matches · two are wrong</strong><br />The crossed matches also give the mug €24 and the bowl €20.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>All four records on the right say O13, so matching on order ID alone connects every product to every price. The missing line numbers held the association we needed. Keeping the full line key allows this split to be joined back without inventing pairs; it does not make splitting these fields useful.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .rejoin.wide { margin-left:50%; }
  .join-options { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:2rem; margin-top:1.5rem; }
  .join-options > div { min-width:0; }
  .join-options h4 { min-height:3rem; }
  .match-pair { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.75rem; }
  .match-drawing { position:relative; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; height:10rem; }
  .match-drawing svg { position:absolute; width:26%; height:100%; left:37%; }
  .match-drawing path { fill:none; stroke:var(--teal); stroke-width:1.5; vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke; }
  .match-drawing .false-match { stroke:var(--coral); stroke-dasharray:4 3; }
  .match-column { width:37%; display:grid; grid-template-rows:1fr 1fr; align-items:center; }
  .match-column :global(.sheet-content) { padding:.6rem .65rem .75rem; }
  .match-column:last-child { text-align:right; }
  .match-column small { display:block; font:.7rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .match-column strong { display:block; font-size:.87rem; font-weight:500; }
  .join-result { font-size:.82rem; border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.7rem; }
  .join-result.wrong { border-color:var(--coral); }
  @media(max-width:400px) { .match-drawing { height:12rem; } }
  @media(max-width:700px) { .join-options { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .join-options h4 { min-height:0; } }
</style>
